#ChatPanel Gateway API

#The ChatPanel gateway runs on the user's machine (loopback only, port 4320 by default). It redacts personal data before a model sees it, routes model traffic, and holds the user's searchable history, durable memory, shared preferences and the team/project run boards.  **It only answers on loopback.** A client on another host cannot reach it; an SDK refuses a non-loopback base URL unless the integrator opts in and uses TLS.  **Two trust levels.** The `/v1` data plane is open to any local process — that is the product. Writes that change what every client sees (remember, forget, ingest) and anything admin-shaped require the per-install token the gateway writes to `~/.chatpanel/gateway-token` (mode 0600), or a copy obtained by pairing (`POST /pair` with a one-time code from `chatpanel-gateway pair`). `POST /whoami` says which trust you have.  **Errors** are `{ error: { message, type } }` (or `{ error: \"text\" }` on the oldest routes) with the HTTP status. `type` is a stable machine word: `not_found`, `invalid_request`, `unknown_endpoint`, `unavailable`, `bridge_unreachable`, `no_bridge`, `redact_error`, `search_error`, `memory_error`, `team_error`, `ingest_error`, `prefs_error`. 

